From 66fcec8069d53cc5397ee69de9d2d9546c736a59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:03:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(usage): tick each usage bar at the share of its
 window that has elapsed

Usage windows carried how much was used and when they reset, but not how
long they are, so nothing could say how far through a window you are.
Add an optional durationSeconds to usage windows and balances, and have the
sources fill it from what the provider establishes: the reported seconds
(Codex, Muse, Kimi), named five-hour and weekly fields (Claude, Grok,
OpenCode Go, Muse), or a reported start and end (MiniMax intervals,
Cursor billing cycles). Calendar months and unreported lengths stay
without one.

The app draws an orange tick on every usage bar where the window can be
placed: cards, balance rows and the sidebar summary. The tick follows the
used/remaining preference, elapsed time beside used and time left beside
remaining, so a fill running past the tick is usage outpacing the clock.
A kept report whose reset has passed gets no tick.

Protocol: the field is optional. Older apps keep parsing (generated
validators pass unknown keys); older daemons omit it and the bars show no
tick.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
